From dd9a8ffaab45fdee85c3e88e31382dad29d4768f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Senior Matthew <SeniorMatt@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 02:22:32 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 22/32] kcm_device_automounter: QtWidgets form reordered
 (option first, device list under a title), clearer column names, device list
 loaded after the first frame

Page type: List (QtWidgets, docs/page-design.md section 8: no port). kcfg keys, per-device settings, save() housekeeping and the kded
module reload are unchanged. Not built yet.

Moved / renamed:
- The checkbox that decides which new devices are mounted moved above the list, now "Also mount devices that have never been
  mounted before" with a hint line under it (kcm_device_automounter/AutomountUnknownDevices; was the last widget, "Automatically
  mount removable media that have never been mounted before").
- The list gets a bold title "Devices" and a one-line hint. Columns "Automount Device / On Login / On Attach" became
  "Device / At Login / When Connected"; branch "Attached Devices" became "Connected Devices" (kcm_device_automounter/deviceView).
- "Forget Device" became "Forget Selected Devices", right-aligned under the list (kcm_device_automounter/forgetDevice).
  Old wording is in the ia/layout.json aliases.
HIG ids: HIG-001/005/006 (order by use), HIG-057, title case on buttons, no jargon ("attach").

Speed cause (DeviceModel.cpp, DeviceAutomounterKCM.cpp): DeviceModel's constructor ran reload() and then load() ran reload() again,
so every known device was enumerated and its config group read twice before the first frame. The constructor call is gone and
load() now schedules the reload and column layout with QTimer::singleShot(0). save() runs the pending reload first
(finishLoad), so the cleanup of removed device groups can never run against an empty model. After numbers: pending, manager
will measure.

Unconfirmed: nothing was compiled or opened; the .ui was only checked as well-formed XML. The whatsThis texts still quote the
old checkbox wording (they already did not match upstream's current text).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
